1. SCOPE

This notice covers everything in this repository and on the website,
including the homepage, "Gravity Slingshot" (gravity-slingshot/) and
"Tianxia" (tianxia/): source code, game rules and mechanics as expressed in
the code and text, level designs, scenario and country data, text, graphics,
layout and documentation (the "Work"). Third-party materials (for example
web fonts loaded from Google Fonts) belong to their respective owners and
are used under their own licenses.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

Only the following uses are permitted:

 (a) Play and view. You may visit the website and play the games in a web
     browser for your own personal, non-commercial use.

 (b) GitHub. You may view and fork this repository on GitHub only to the
     extent GitHub's Terms of Service require. A fork receives no rights
     beyond that; in particular it may not be deployed as a website, used,
     modified or redistributed outside GitHub.

 (c) Tianxia relay proxy. You may copy and run the file tianxia/ai-proxy.mjs
     (for example as a Cloudflare Worker or on your own computer), and change
     its configuration, solely so that you and the people you play with can
     use the Tianxia game at https://zechenbian.github.io/tianxia/. Any other
     use or redistribution of that file is not permitted.

 (d) Citation. You may quote brief excerpts with attribution for commentary,
     review, teaching or academic citation, to the extent permitted by law.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Except as stated in Section 2, you may not, without the prior written
permission of the copyright holder:

 - copy, reproduce, download for redistribution, mirror or re-host the Work
   or any part of it;
 - modify, translate, adapt, port or create derivative works from the Work,
   including clones or re-implementations that reproduce its levels, data,
   rules text or other protected expression;
 - distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent or otherwise make the Work
   available to others, whether free of charge or not;
 - use the Work, in whole or in part, for any commercial purpose;
 - use the Work, in whole or in part, to train, fine-tune, evaluate or
   benchmark any machine-learning or artificial-intelligence model, or
   include it in any dataset, corpus or retrieval index for such purposes,
   including by automated crawling or scraping;
 - remove, obscure or alter any copyright notice or this license.

